    {
      "question": "e-477",
      "field": null,
      "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
      "old_sha256": "11bf4cbdc00d8438bd494b22f15cc5534dc7dbea0ffae5fc93212619d660f60c",
      "new_sha256": "01a404fe2ba8339d8d1d9469de55c8e1ce083ccc0435e78efb95b42e6bec5df9",
      "category": "ma_capture",
      "authoring": [],
      "source": [
        {
          "question": "e-477",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "We use a variation of the Pythagorean identity:\n\n$$\n\\sin^2 x + \\cos^2 x = 1\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad  \\cos^2 x = 1-\\sin^2 x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we rewrite the denominator and calculate the resulting integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{1-{sin}^{2}\u2061x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}\u2061x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {(\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x})}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {sec}^{2}\u2061x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tan}\u2061x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/example-477.json",
          "file_sha256": "33a6fb5067d0a9efaf01c1f5cedcb1ea3a49856e6344dcc1c050d26e6b496184"
        }
      ],
