    {
      "question": "e-479",
      "field": null,
      "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
      "old_sha256": "29843a8795697691906a1d67c1f4afdb51a13046671b06fa3c4ef8cd588e96e6",
      "new_sha256": "0c7f2126c037d4ffdafd931bd74ced5ff5684c97ab604bafe8b1cd08543bbb0a",
      "category": "ma_capture",
      "authoring": [],
      "source": [
        {
          "question": "e-479",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "In this case, we have to use the identity  $1+\\cot^2x =\\csc^2 x.$ Rearranging this gives\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\cot^2 x &=\\csc^2 x -1.\n}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral gives\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\int \\left(5\\cot^2 x -x^2\\right) \\, \\textrm{d}x&=\\int \\bigg(5\\left(\\csc^2 x -1 \\right) -x^2\\bigg) \\, \\textrm{d}x\\\n\t\t\t\t&=\\int \\left(5\\csc^2 x -5 -x^2\\right ) \\, \\textrm{d}x\\\n\t\t\t\t&=-5\\cot x -5x-\\dfrac{x^3}{3}+C.\t\n\t}\n$$",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007646/example-479.json",
          "file_sha256": "39c8e5a4f8461de8bb14161ec0e580a0d969324edd6bf19157b6e231fc7ee934"
        }
